  {"h": "Match the bed, then ignore the label",
   "body": "The T1 Silverado's beds are 69.9, 79.4 and 98.2 in long at the floor. Chevrolet dealers call them the short, standard and long bed. Cover makers don't agree on names: RealTruck calls the short bed 5'8\", while BAK and Tyger list the same part as 5'10\" (69.9\"). The inch figure in the listing title is the one to trust. If you're unsure, measure from the front bulkhead to the inside of the closed tailgate. A cover sized for the wrong bed won't seal at the tailgate and will leak at the back corners, and no aftermarket kit fixes that. The short bed comes only on the Crew Cab, the standard bed on Double Cab and Crew Cab, and the long bed on the Regular Cab."},
  {"h": "The 2019 LD and 2022 LTD traps",
   "body": "GM sold two different trucks as the 2019 Silverado 1500. The LD (sold as Limited or Legacy in listings) was the third-generation truck, built alongside the new T1, and its bed matches the 2014–2018 truck. Covers for it are listed \"2014–2018, 2019 Limited/Legacy\" and won't fit a T1. For 2022 the naming flipped: the Silverado 1500 LTD was the pre-refresh T1, the same as a 2021, so it takes 2019+ covers. Check the window sticker or registration for LD or LTD before you order. A seller's fitment tool that only asks for the model year can't tell these trucks apart, so pick the body style yourself."},
  {"h": "Multi-Flex tailgate: supported, with one catch",
   "body": "Chevrolet added the Multi-Flex six-function tailgate to the 2021 Silverado 1500, available from WT to High Country, after GMC launched it as MultiPro on the 2019 Sierra. BAK, Retrax, TruXedo and UnderCover all list their Silverado covers as working with or without it. The cover seals on top of the tailgate, so the main gate drops normally. The inner gate is different: with a folding cover latched, the rear panel sits over it. Fold that panel forward before using the step or inner load stop. GM rates the Multi-Flex step at 375 lb, and it's worth keeping usable."},
  {"h": "Power tailgates and storage boxes",
   "body": "Two factory options rule covers out. GM's in-bed side storage boxes occupy the rail space where clamps go, and every RealTruck fitment note on this page says the cover won't work with them. Power tailgates are the second. GM offered power-down and power up/down gates on the T1, the latter on LTZ and High Country, and Tyger states the T3 interferes with a power tailgate. Multi-Flex trucks don't have power operation, since GM made the two mutually exclusive. If yours has either option, confirm fitment before you buy. A box-compatible cover is a different product category altogether."},
